acceptance_criteria: Exported typed adapter API; no git on source paths; coherent real filesystem revision or typed refusal under race; strict RFC 6901 pointers; size/deadline/cancellation bounds
parent: pm-evidence-build
comments[4]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-23T07:53:26.152Z",codex-agent,"Real filesystem race barrier changed a source after discovery and before open: refused mixed revisions; stable subsequent read had the exact expected SHA-256. Replacement, growth, invalid UTF-8, BOM preservation, unreadable files, custom adapter deadlines and cancellation are covered without SDK mocks."
  "2026-10-23T08:30:01.382Z",codex-agent,"PR 1 blocking review: verify the opened descriptor target through Linux procfs and its device/inode, before reading, so parent symlink swaps cannot escape the selected root. Fail closed when descriptor verification is unavailable; document the Linux platform boundary. Add a deterministic real-filesystem parent-swap regression and function-only revert proof."
  "2026-10-23T08:51:09.851Z",codex-agent,"PR 1 descriptor-containment revert proof: changed only verifyDescriptor to the prior unverified no-op behavior while keeping real filesystem swap/restore barriers active. The regression failed 1 test because an external descriptor was accepted as current after parent symlink swap and pathname restoration. Restored source byte-for-byte. Positive tests verify before/after-read kernel descriptor containment, device/inode identity, closed-descriptor refusal and unsupported-platform refusal. Linux procfs is required; no weaker path-only fallback exists."
  "2026-10-23T15:21:11.044Z",codex-agent,"DELIVERED: merged PR #1 (210cc3a319d3f61b4bad69fecbcb741dac61aa7b) is an ancestor of audited main 1bb9e2bfebdde13041e75f5fa9889a97ed577052. Inspected on main: test/sources.test.ts, test/selectors.test.ts, src/types.ts. Exported typed adapters, gitless source paths, coherent filesystem read-or-refusal, strict RFC6901 pointers, deadlines/cancellation and bounds are covered, including descriptor-swap refusal. This tracker audit inspected existing tests/files; it does not claim a new full product test run."
